	(text "X201 50.000 MHz CMOS oscillator (ECS-2520MV-500-BN-TR: +/-50 ppm, -40 to +85 C, 8.0 mA max at 3.3 V)\n-> R209 -> PCLKT0_1 (pin 128; FPGA-TN-02154 section 13: single-ended clocks on PCLKT pins only).\nSupply filter per FPGA-TN-02154 Figure 13.1: FB201 600 ohm bead, C225 0.1 uF, C226 1 uF on VDD_OSC.\nOE (pin 1) tied to VDD_OSC: always running (>= 0.7 Vdd = active). 15 pF maximum load per the data sheet."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 431.8 213.36 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "1342a638-ebf7-5d6e-8774-b452bd6b005e")
	)
	(text "POWER (data sheet Table 3.2: HC core VCC 2.375-3.6 V, VCCIO 1.14-3.6 V): VCC and every VCCIO bank on the\nsame +3V3 supply (Table 3.2 note 1: like supplies tied together); all banks LVCMOS33. Sheet 5: ramp 0.01-100 V/ms\n(Table 3.3); regulator within 3% (FPGA-TN-02154 section 2.2).\nNC pin 129 not connected (pinout file). Pins 31, 63, 103 are I/O pads on the\nLCMXO2-4000HC only (NC on the 2000HC): kept spare and unconnected, so the G-SHEET2 assignment is unchanged (C-30)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 172.72 264.16 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2652599a-d9f0-54f4-b193-57d21829e256")
	)
	(text "DESIGN NOTES (summary; full analysis in docs/stage2/sheet2-design-notes.md)\n1. Every signal pin comes from tools/fpga/pinplan.py (also the LPF LOCATEs and docs/stage2/sheet2-pin-assignment.md).\n   Bank 1 holds the whole /SLAVEn, XRDY and buffer-enable decode group (C-01/C-02 paths).\n2. Owner decisions C-17 and C-26 (option C-17b): 101 signals; PROGRAMN/INITN/DONE and JTAG kept; JTAGENB unused (C-19).\n   Only the READY LED is on the FPGA; FAULT and the other diagnostic LEDs are on the RP2040.\n   C-30 (2026-11-19): LCMXO2-4000HC-4TG144C. The G-SHEET2 pins are unchanged (tools/fpga/pinplan.py also checks them\n   against the 2000 pinout file); 6 spare: 23, 24, 67 and the 4000-only pads 31, 63, 103.\n3. Post-place-and-route STA with the complete design (sheet 4, LCMXO2-4000HC, both grades, 15 pF): every constraint\n   met; worst Zorro path 14.773 ns of 18; /SLAVEn at the slot 21.92 ns of 35; M-7 >= 19.8 ns (sheet4-sta-results.md).\n4. Interfaces: sheet 1 (ZB_*, ZF_*, EN_OK, LD*), sheet 3 (SA*, SRAM_*, LD*), sheet 4 (RP_*, FPGA_TCK/TMS/TDI/TDO),\n   sheet 5 (I2C_*, INA_ALERT_N, X4_*), sheet 6 (LED_READY, DIP_*, DBG*). Sheets 5-6 are not yet drawn.\n5. Erased-device rules (FPGA-TN-02155 section 6): the I2C configuration port on pins 125/126 ACKs 7-bit\n   addresses 0x40-0x43, so no telemetry device on I2C_SDA/I2C_SCL may use them (sheet 5). SN is never driven low.\n   SDA/SCL are limited to -0.25..3.75 V (data sheet Table 3.1 note 5): I2C pull-ups to +3V3 only.\n6. Back-powering (FPGA-TN-02154 section 14): no FPGA input may be driven while +3V3 is off. Sheets 1 and 3 comply\n   (Ioff / VCC-isolated buffers, pull-ups to +3V3), and so does sheet 4; sheets 5-6 must keep it (debug header, X4 sense).\n7. Erased or unconfigured FPGA: every Zorro-side output is held inactive by its sheet-1 resistor and ZF_ARM is pulled\n   low, so the card is disabled and the slot looks empty; SRAM deselected (R301/R302). Hardware check M-14.\n8. Not yet validated: an ERC-clean result does not imply electrical or timing correctness."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 355.6 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "89c32c32-642f-5826-adb2-5cd0c80e3423")
	)
	(text "CONFIGURATION (FPGA-TN-02154 section 6, Table 6.1, Figure 6.1): PROGRAMN, INITN, DONE kept as\nconfiguration pins (SYSCONFIG SDM_PORT=PROGRAMN_DONE_INITN), 4.7k pull-ups to VCCIO0. JTAG port enabled.\nJTAGENB: no signal (C-19), 1k pull-up = JTAG mode, so JTAG stays available whatever the bitstream.\nTCK 4.7k pull-down; TMS, TDI, TDO 4.7k pull-ups. SN (pin 70) carries SA17, an FPGA output: 4.7k\npull-up to VCCIO2 keeps SN high while the device is erased (\"ensure SN and PROGRAMN are not driven low\")."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 304.8 104.14 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "a9e0eca5-7c02-59d4-8a3b-49dca9d5b806")
	)
	(text "J201 JTAG (programming, boundary scan). PROJECT PIN ORDER, not a vendor standard:\n1 VREF (+3V3)  2 GND  3 TCK  4 TDO  5 TDI  6 TMS.\nPolarized KK 254 header: the mating housing fits one way only. PCB silkscreen:\nthe signal name at every pin, a pin-1 marker and \"JTAG 3V3\".\nVREF = carrier +3V3, so a programmer never powers the board. The RP2040 JTAG\noption (D-12) joins these nets on sheet 4 via a translator enabled by a DIP\nswitch (sheet 6)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 330.2 170.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bc1ce575-4489-572f-ae3c-5c1db7d973ae")
	)
	(text "DECOUPLING (Lattice FPGA-TN-02154 Table 3.1): VCC 2 x 10 uF + 100 nF per pin (4 pins);\nVCCIO 10 uF per bank + 100 nF per pin (12 pins, 6 banks). 100 nF at each pin on the PCB."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 304.8 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "bfc982c8-2d94-59d1-b095-5f44c231e92d")
	)
